+++ b/dylib/tests/activation.md
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Cooperative launch activation controls
+
+`make activation-relay` builds small native applications and exercises the actual
+activation relay with only the two Steam frontend identities replaced by private
+test identities. It never loads code into Steam or launches a game. The activation
+source uses production memory-management flags; the test app uses ARC.
+
+Run on an unlocked macOS desktop without another Wine session. The controls change
+focus for about a minute; do not interact with their windows. Each application exits
+on its own. Receipts, source/binary hashes and native callback logs are retained in
+`out/activation-*`. Missing callbacks, unexpected application switches and incomplete
+results fail rather than being counted as success.
+
+The detached no-handoff baseline must remain inactive. A ready helper must grant
+activation for immediate and delayed windows. Blocking the helper's main queue
+must demonstrate acknowledgement before spawning, not success by a repeated lucky
+timing. An absent receiver must time out within the bounded interval and continue
+without activation. A deliberate switch during delayed creation must keep the
+other app active. Requests, acknowledgements, application activation and key-window
+callbacks are recorded separately.
+
+These controls reproduce the native handoff mechanism. They do not establish game
+rendering, input, fullscreen presentation, Wine minimization behavior, or acceptance
+on a different macOS version. Validate those through ordinary owner-led Steam
+launches with the installed candidate and again without temporary diagnostics.
